1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:01,254
The plain figure takes

2
00:00:01,254 --> 00:00:02,562
one step toward the door.

3
00:00:02,562 --> 00:00:04,933
The blanket slides off its shoulders.

4
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:06,122
It stops on the doorstep,

5
00:00:06,122 --> 00:00:07,689
and looks out across the ice.

6
00:00:07,689 --> 00:00:08,559
At the gap.

7
00:00:08,559 --> 00:00:10,153
At the single circle.

8
00:00:10,153 --> 00:00:12,155
At the striped figure,

9
00:00:12,155 --> 00:00:14,880
standing beside its own silver case, waiting.

10
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,063
You don't breathe.

11
00:00:16,063 --> 00:00:17,276
Neither does Mara.

12
00:00:17,276 --> 00:00:18,980
Then it turns around.

13
00:00:19,497 --> 00:00:21,043
It picks up the blanket,

14
00:00:21,043 --> 00:00:22,528
walks back to the fire,

15
00:00:22,528 --> 00:00:25,153
and sits down with its back to the door.

16
00:00:25,153 --> 00:00:26,616
Almost the way Mara sat

17
00:00:26,616 --> 00:00:29,305
down on the hilltop, on day 91.

18
00:00:29,919 --> 00:00:31,542
Mara lets out a breath that

19
00:00:31,542 --> 00:00:33,164
sounds almost like a laugh.

20
00:00:33,164 --> 00:00:36,315
You know exactly what she's thinking.

21
00:00:36,315 --> 00:00:38,746
Sixty days ago, you sat on a hilltop and

22
00:00:38,746 --> 00:00:40,950
watched a gap you wouldn't walk through.

23
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:43,330
Now you're on the other side of the door,

24
00:00:43,703 --> 00:00:45,917
watching somebody else refuse.

25
00:00:45,917 --> 00:00:48,074
Outside, nothing changes.

26
00:00:48,448 --> 00:00:50,666
The striped figure waits all morning.

27
00:00:50,666 --> 00:00:51,841
All afternoon.

28
00:00:52,358 --> 00:00:53,962
At dusk, you wait for the

29
00:00:53,962 --> 00:00:56,412
soft sound of a page being turned.

30
00:00:56,412 --> 00:00:57,703
It doesn't come.

31
00:00:57,703 --> 00:00:59,523
The gap stays open.

32
00:00:59,914 --> 00:01:02,009
The single circle keeps glowing,

33
00:01:02,009 --> 00:01:04,474
all night, pale on the ice.

34
00:01:04,474 --> 00:01:07,784
And the striped figure stands beside it,

35
00:01:07,784 --> 00:01:10,554
in the cold, without moving, until morning.

36
00:01:11,137 --> 00:01:12,422
Every time you wake up,

37
00:01:12,422 --> 00:01:14,488
you look out of the loft window.

38
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:16,724
Every time, it's still there.

39
00:01:16,724 --> 00:01:19,326
Snow settles on its shoulders,

40
00:01:19,326 --> 00:01:21,958
on the stripe, on the case at its feet.

41
00:01:21,958 --> 00:01:23,530
It doesn't brush it off.

42
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:24,303
On the hill,

43
00:01:24,303 --> 00:01:27,205
they closed the door when you said no.

44
00:01:27,205 --> 00:01:29,956
This time, somebody is leaving it open.

45
00:01:29,956 --> 00:01:31,089
On day 152,

46
00:01:31,089 --> 00:01:34,933
the plain figure eats its last cube.

47
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:36,713
It takes a long time about it.

48
00:01:36,713 --> 00:01:38,851
Then it shows you the empty pocket,

49
00:01:38,851 --> 00:01:40,814
the way it showed you the full one.

50
00:01:40,814 --> 00:01:43,343
Mara finds the column in the ledger.

51
00:01:43,343 --> 00:01:44,538
Its food: four.

52
00:01:44,538 --> 00:01:46,899
Underneath, she writes: none.

53
00:01:46,899 --> 00:01:49,673
You don't have a cube to give it.

54
00:01:49,673 --> 00:01:51,521
You don't have anything it can eat.

55
00:01:51,521 --> 00:01:52,291
You have snow,

56
00:01:52,291 --> 00:01:55,264
which you melt in the kettle, and a fire,

57
00:01:55,264 --> 00:01:58,266
which you feed one crate slat at a time.

58
00:01:58,266 --> 00:01:59,487
So you give it those.

59
00:01:59,487 --> 00:02:01,934
You sit with it by the fire that night,

60
00:02:01,934 --> 00:02:02,826
the three of you,

61
00:02:02,826 --> 00:02:05,291
and nobody pretends this is fine.

62
00:02:05,906 --> 00:02:07,854
Mara says it's doing what you did.

63
00:02:07,854 --> 00:02:09,546
It's refusing to choose.

64
00:02:09,985 --> 00:02:11,712
You say it isn't the same.

65
00:02:11,712 --> 00:02:12,543
On the hill,

66
00:02:12,543 --> 00:02:14,897
you had each other inside the ring.

67
00:02:14,897 --> 00:02:17,316
Its other is outside, on the ice.

68
00:02:17,786 --> 00:02:19,328
You both look at the window.

69
00:02:19,328 --> 00:02:21,638
The striped figure is still there,

70
00:02:21,638 --> 00:02:23,208
a dark shape against the snow,

71
00:02:23,208 --> 00:02:24,875
beside the glowing circle.

72
00:02:25,249 --> 00:02:26,597
It hasn't eaten either,

73
00:02:26,597 --> 00:02:27,945
as far as you can tell.

74
00:02:27,945 --> 00:02:29,375
It hasn't sat down.

75
00:02:29,375 --> 00:02:32,035
You've feared that figure for

76
00:02:32,035 --> 00:02:33,279
a hundred and fifty-two days.

77
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:35,287
The scanner through the walls.

78
00:02:35,287 --> 00:02:37,275
The line that stopped on you.

79
00:02:37,275 --> 00:02:39,768
It never once occurred to you that

80
00:02:39,768 --> 00:02:41,935
it might be waiting for someone, too.

81
00:02:42,567 --> 00:02:43,590
On day 154,

82
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:47,072
the plain figure explains why it won't go.

83
00:02:47,072 --> 00:02:48,220
Its hand shakes,

84
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:50,477
so the drawing comes slowly.

85
00:02:50,916 --> 00:02:52,763
First, the stadium ring,

86
00:02:52,763 --> 00:02:54,314
with pairs inside it,

87
00:02:54,314 --> 00:02:57,896
and a small craft over it, and an arrow, up.

88
00:02:58,543 --> 00:03:00,035
Then the ring on the ice,

89
00:03:00,035 --> 00:03:01,717
with the mill inside it.

90
00:03:02,156 --> 00:03:05,619
And above it, a craft, and an arrow, up.

91
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:07,822
Then it copies the number from the

92
00:03:07,822 --> 00:03:09,909
top of your roll, the one in the box.

93
00:03:09,909 --> 00:03:10,420
180.

94
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:13,656
You understand before it finishes.

95
00:03:13,656 --> 00:03:15,508
Every ring you've seen is a

96
00:03:15,508 --> 00:03:18,462
place where people wait to be lifted.

97
00:03:18,462 --> 00:03:19,292
The stadium.

98
00:03:19,292 --> 00:03:20,460
The mast.

99
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:21,377
The park.

100
00:03:21,377 --> 00:03:23,302
And now, this island.

101
00:03:23,302 --> 00:03:24,616
On day 180,

102
00:03:24,616 --> 00:03:27,600
whatever is inside a ring goes up.

103
00:03:27,943 --> 00:03:30,620
The plain figure draws one more thing.

104
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:33,661
Itself, walking out through the gap.

105
00:03:33,661 --> 00:03:35,915
Behind it, the gap closing.

106
00:03:35,915 --> 00:03:37,899
And inside the ring,

107
00:03:37,899 --> 00:03:40,883
two small figures, one with a scarf.

108
00:03:40,883 --> 00:03:43,715
Then it draws a hard line through itself.

109
00:03:43,715 --> 00:03:46,184
It isn't staying because it's stubborn.

110
00:03:46,622 --> 00:03:48,971
It's staying because the moment it leaves,

111
00:03:48,971 --> 00:03:51,241
the ring closes around you.

112
00:03:51,241 --> 00:03:52,778
And on day 180,

113
00:03:52,778 --> 00:03:55,563
you go up with the island.

114
00:03:55,563 --> 00:03:57,492
You could walk out, of course.

115
00:03:57,492 --> 00:03:59,059
The band isn't a wall.

116
00:03:59,059 --> 00:04:01,169
But out there is a frozen river,

117
00:04:01,169 --> 00:04:04,231
a white country, and no roof for miles.

118
00:04:04,231 --> 00:04:05,470
And in here,

119
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:08,613
by your fire, is the only one of them who

120
00:04:08,613 --> 00:04:10,636
ever wiped away your footprints.

121
00:04:10,636 --> 00:04:13,097
You don't even say it out loud.

122
00:04:13,097 --> 00:04:15,582
You just put another slat on the fire.

123
00:04:15,582 --> 00:04:18,735
Mara puts her hand flat on the drawing.

124
00:04:18,735 --> 00:04:20,510
Two, whatever happens.

125
00:04:20,965 --> 00:04:23,338
It was a promise between the two of you.

126
00:04:23,338 --> 00:04:24,881
You never thought anyone

127
00:04:24,881 --> 00:04:27,947
else would keep it for you.

128
00:04:27,947 --> 00:04:29,561
On day 157,

129
00:04:29,870 --> 00:04:31,768
you start burning the mill.

130
00:04:31,768 --> 00:04:34,222
The firewood ran out two days ago.

131
00:04:34,222 --> 00:04:36,972
First, the little shop counter.

132
00:04:37,474 --> 00:04:40,566
Then the ladder to the loft you don't use.

133
00:04:41,405 --> 00:04:42,764
Then the handrail of the stairs,

134
00:04:42,764 --> 00:04:45,281
which you'll miss on the way down in the dark.

135
00:04:45,281 --> 00:04:47,246
The hand saw gets warm from working.

136
00:04:47,246 --> 00:04:49,518
That's the only thing that does.

137
00:04:49,518 --> 00:04:51,802
You sleep in every piece of clothing you own,

138
00:04:51,802 --> 00:04:53,385
both of you under one blanket,

139
00:04:53,385 --> 00:04:55,962
with the other one around the plain figure.

140
00:04:56,496 --> 00:04:57,304
In the mornings,

141
00:04:57,304 --> 00:04:59,474
there's frost on the inside of the window.

142
00:04:59,474 --> 00:05:02,092
You cut a hole in the ice beside the island wall,

143
00:05:02,092 --> 00:05:03,342
with the saw and a great

144
00:05:03,342 --> 00:05:06,131
deal of language Mara pretends not to hear.

145
00:05:06,131 --> 00:05:08,289
Black water wells up in it.

146
00:05:08,289 --> 00:05:09,852
Mara drops the fishing line in,

147
00:05:09,852 --> 00:05:11,164
and that evening,

148
00:05:11,164 --> 00:05:13,039
there are two small fish on the fire.

149
00:05:13,039 --> 00:05:15,236
You count the food while they cook.

150
00:05:15,236 --> 00:05:16,363
Four potatoes.

151
00:05:16,363 --> 00:05:17,866
Three bags of oats.

152
00:05:17,866 --> 00:05:19,293
Three of flour.

153
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:20,469
Eight tins.

154
00:05:20,469 --> 00:05:21,593
Nine candles.

155
00:05:21,593 --> 00:05:22,716
And two fish,

156
00:05:22,716 --> 00:05:24,991
which won't be on the list for long.

157
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:26,237
While you sit by the hole,

158
00:05:26,237 --> 00:05:28,122
you hear something you've been

159
00:05:28,122 --> 00:05:29,727
hearing for weeks without listening.

160
00:05:29,727 --> 00:05:30,747
Under the ice,

161
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:33,182
under the weir, the river is still running.

162
00:05:33,557 --> 00:05:34,653
Roaring, actually.

163
00:05:34,653 --> 00:05:35,173
Muffled,

164
00:05:35,173 --> 00:05:37,812
like it's shouting in another room.

165
00:05:37,812 --> 00:05:39,015
The river isn't frozen.

166
00:05:39,015 --> 00:05:40,568
It's just wearing a lid.

167
00:05:41,569 --> 00:05:45,175
On day 160, the plain figure can't get up.

168
00:05:45,582 --> 00:05:48,185
You find it lying on its side by the fire,

169
00:05:48,185 --> 00:05:50,638
its face gone the color of ashes.

170
00:05:50,638 --> 00:05:52,126
It isn't moving much.

171
00:05:52,885 --> 00:05:54,763
Mara looks at it for a long time.

172
00:05:54,763 --> 00:05:56,444
Then she takes the roll,

173
00:05:56,818 --> 00:05:59,173
the page with two joined circles,

174
00:05:59,173 --> 00:06:03,537
one striped and one plain, and walks out into the snow.

175
00:06:03,537 --> 00:06:05,711
Right to the edge of the ring.

176
00:06:05,711 --> 00:06:06,885
You know what she's going

177
00:06:06,885 --> 00:06:08,392
to do before she does it.

178
00:06:08,392 --> 00:06:10,687
She did it on day 75.

179
00:06:10,687 --> 00:06:12,166
She calls out.

180
00:06:12,166 --> 00:06:15,018
Her voice cracks across the frozen river.

181
00:06:15,018 --> 00:06:16,928
It's the loudest thing anyone

182
00:06:16,928 --> 00:06:19,123
has said on this island in weeks.

183
00:06:19,464 --> 00:06:21,439
The striped figure turns its head.

184
00:06:21,439 --> 00:06:23,263
Mara holds up the drawing.

185
00:06:23,637 --> 00:06:24,577
The striped figure

186
00:06:24,577 --> 00:06:26,312
looks at it for a long time.

187
00:06:26,846 --> 00:06:27,990
Then it does something

188
00:06:27,990 --> 00:06:29,682
none of them has ever done.

189
00:06:30,136 --> 00:06:31,642
It steps through the gap.

190
00:06:31,642 --> 00:06:32,811
Into the ring.

191
00:06:33,506 --> 00:06:35,421
It walks straight past Mara,

192
00:06:35,421 --> 00:06:37,827
up the island, into the mill,

193
00:06:37,827 --> 00:06:40,757
and kneels on the floor beside the plain figure.

194
00:06:41,292 --> 00:06:43,246
From a pocket on its own suit,

195
00:06:43,246 --> 00:06:44,932
it takes a pale cube.

196
00:06:45,483 --> 00:06:46,908
It breaks it in half.

197
00:06:46,908 --> 00:06:49,722
It gives one half to the plain figure,

198
00:06:49,722 --> 00:06:51,052
and it keeps the other.

199
00:06:51,052 --> 00:06:52,438
Then it sits down on the

200
00:06:52,438 --> 00:06:54,810
floor beside it, and stays there.

201
00:06:54,810 --> 00:06:56,308
You and Mara stand by the

202
00:06:56,308 --> 00:06:57,916
wall and don't say a word.

203
00:06:57,916 --> 00:06:59,129
There are two of them

204
00:06:59,129 --> 00:07:01,026
by your fire tonight.

205
00:07:01,026 --> 00:07:02,358
You've never felt so much

206
00:07:02,358 --> 00:07:04,246
like a guest in your own home.

207
00:07:04,717 --> 00:07:07,075
By morning, the striped figure is back

208
00:07:07,075 --> 00:07:09,836
outside the gap, as if nothing happened.

209
00:07:09,836 --> 00:07:12,077
But the plain figure can sit up.

210
00:07:12,419 --> 00:07:16,154
On day 163, the ship starts to move.

211
00:07:16,463 --> 00:07:17,337
Since day 85,

212
00:07:17,337 --> 00:07:20,443
it has hung over the hill and the mast,

213
00:07:20,443 --> 00:07:23,216
far behind you, on the horizon.

214
00:07:23,216 --> 00:07:25,542
Now its straight edge creeps

215
00:07:25,542 --> 00:07:28,109
across the sky, a little more every hour.

216
00:07:28,482 --> 00:07:30,152
Toward the river.

217
00:07:30,152 --> 00:07:31,265
Toward you.

218
00:07:31,265 --> 00:07:33,065
By the afternoon,

219
00:07:33,065 --> 00:07:35,727
it covers the far bend, and the trees on the

220
00:07:35,727 --> 00:07:38,502
far bank have no shadows anymore.

221
00:07:38,502 --> 00:07:39,827
Every evening now,

222
00:07:39,827 --> 00:07:43,150
the striped figure comes into the mill.

223
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:44,221
Every evening,

224
00:07:44,221 --> 00:07:47,066
it breaks one cube, and gives half away.

225
00:07:47,066 --> 00:07:50,174
It never looks at you while it does it.

226
00:07:50,174 --> 00:07:52,179
You never look at it, either.

227
00:07:52,179 --> 00:07:54,718
It seems like the polite thing to do.

228
00:07:54,718 --> 00:07:56,963
It's grayer than it was, too.

229
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:58,489
Slower to kneel.

230
00:07:58,489 --> 00:07:59,938
You do the arithmetic,

231
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:02,015
because you can't stop.

232
00:08:02,015 --> 00:08:03,035
Two aliens.

233
00:08:03,035 --> 00:08:04,354
One pocket.

234
00:08:04,729 --> 00:08:05,975
Half rations.

235
00:08:05,975 --> 00:08:07,343
Four potatoes,

236
00:08:07,718 --> 00:08:10,042
then three, then two.

237
00:08:10,042 --> 00:08:12,995
On day 42, you watched the stadium

238
00:08:12,995 --> 00:08:13,940
from a footbridge,

239
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:17,463
and wondered what kind of creatures could take people away.

240
00:08:17,463 --> 00:08:20,228
Tonight, two of them sit by your fire,

241
00:08:20,228 --> 00:08:21,785
sharing their last food,

242
00:08:21,785 --> 00:08:23,961
because one of them won't leave you.

243
00:08:23,961 --> 00:08:26,139
And the other one won't leave it.

244
00:08:26,594 --> 00:08:28,260
You write it in the ledger.

245
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:30,523
Nobody here is counting anymore.

246
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:32,444
Everybody is

247
00:08:32,444 --> 00:08:34,737
waiting for somebody.

248
00:08:34,737 --> 00:08:37,978
On day 166, the last loads begin.

249
00:08:37,978 --> 00:08:40,146
From the mill window,

250
00:08:40,146 --> 00:08:42,945
you watch people come across the frozen river.

251
00:08:42,945 --> 00:08:44,213
Not one or two.

252
00:08:44,213 --> 00:08:44,958
Dozens.

253
00:08:44,958 --> 00:08:46,890
From the village,

254
00:08:46,890 --> 00:08:50,049
from the woods, from places you've never seen,

255
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,745
walking on the ice in pairs.

256
00:08:52,745 --> 00:08:55,803
They follow a line of joined circles,

257
00:08:55,803 --> 00:08:57,442
glowing one after another,

258
00:08:57,442 --> 00:08:59,753
to a huge ring of light at the bend,

259
00:08:59,753 --> 00:09:01,904
right under the edge of the ship.

260
00:09:01,904 --> 00:09:04,518
Small craft settle into the ring.

261
00:09:04,518 --> 00:09:05,997
The pairs walk to them.

262
00:09:05,997 --> 00:09:07,283
The craft lift.

263
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:09,181
Then more pairs come.

264
00:09:09,181 --> 00:09:10,769
You watch all day.

265
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,554
You count fourteen craft

266
00:09:12,554 --> 00:09:14,766
before it gets too dark to see.

267
00:09:14,766 --> 00:09:16,747
Some of them carry bags,

268
00:09:16,747 --> 00:09:18,111
the way you carry yours.

269
00:09:18,111 --> 00:09:20,070
Some of them hold hands.

270
00:09:20,070 --> 00:09:21,119
Nobody waves.

271
00:09:21,119 --> 00:09:22,842
Nobody looks back.

272
00:09:23,601 --> 00:09:24,890
Mara stands at the window

273
00:09:24,890 --> 00:09:26,956
long after the light is gone.

274
00:09:26,956 --> 00:09:28,815
On day 75, she called out to two

275
00:09:28,815 --> 00:09:31,901
strangers on the railway, and one of them waved.

276
00:09:31,901 --> 00:09:33,353
They're up there somewhere,

277
00:09:33,353 --> 00:09:35,845
in one of those rows of tiny circles.

278
00:09:35,845 --> 00:09:39,076
So, probably, are the man with the suitcase,

279
00:09:39,076 --> 00:09:40,333
and everyone who ever

280
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:43,880
walked the lit roads past the station.

281
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:45,562
Fourteen days left.

282
00:09:45,562 --> 00:09:48,312
On day 169, Mara has an idea.

283
00:09:48,312 --> 00:09:50,834
She's sitting by the hole in the ice,

284
00:09:51,192 --> 00:09:53,956
listening to the river roar underneath.

285
00:09:53,956 --> 00:09:56,009
She asks you a question.

286
00:09:56,009 --> 00:09:57,289
Why did the band stop

287
00:09:57,289 --> 00:09:58,986
at the water, on day 82?

288
00:09:59,456 --> 00:10:00,793
You say you don't know.

289
00:10:00,793 --> 00:10:02,597
She says neither does she,

290
00:10:02,923 --> 00:10:05,053
but she knows when it stopped stopping.

291
00:10:05,053 --> 00:10:07,351
When the water stopped moving.

292
00:10:07,351 --> 00:10:09,146
The band can lie on ice.

293
00:10:09,146 --> 00:10:11,703
Can it lie on a river that's running?

294
00:10:11,703 --> 00:10:12,637
So you test it,

295
00:10:12,637 --> 00:10:14,750
the way you test everything.

296
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:17,198
You fill the kettle with boiling water,

297
00:10:17,604 --> 00:10:19,700
carry it to the edge of the ring,

298
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:22,940
and pour it on the ice, right where the band lies.

299
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:23,943
The ice hisses,

300
00:10:23,943 --> 00:10:26,541
and melts into a shallow puddle.

301
00:10:26,541 --> 00:10:27,801
And over the puddle,

302
00:10:27,801 --> 00:10:30,319
the band flickers, and goes out.

303
00:10:30,319 --> 00:10:31,637
For about a minute.

304
00:10:31,637 --> 00:10:33,968
Then the puddle freezes again,

305
00:10:33,968 --> 00:10:36,934
and the light comes back, as if nothing happened.

306
00:10:36,934 --> 00:10:38,796
Mara writes it down,

307
00:10:38,796 --> 00:10:40,907
and doesn't add observed.

308
00:10:40,907 --> 00:10:43,081
She writes: moving water.

309
00:10:43,081 --> 00:10:44,769
You go down to the ground

310
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:47,393
floor and look at the mill channel.

311
00:10:47,393 --> 00:10:47,978
At the top,

312
00:10:47,978 --> 00:10:51,145
where the river comes in, there's a sluice gate.

313
00:10:51,145 --> 00:10:52,308
A heavy wooden gate,

314
00:10:52,308 --> 00:10:54,727
set in the stone, with an iron rack and

315
00:10:54,727 --> 00:10:57,266
a big iron wheel to wind it up.

316
00:10:57,266 --> 00:10:58,374
It's frozen solid.

317
00:10:58,374 --> 00:10:59,598
If you could open it,

318
00:10:59,598 --> 00:11:02,453
the whole river would push through the channel.

319
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:03,801
All that roaring water,

320
00:11:03,801 --> 00:11:05,039
under all that ice.

321
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:07,241
It wouldn't stay a lid for long.

322
00:11:07,614 --> 00:11:10,740
And where the ice breaks, the ring breaks.

323
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:11,864
You try the wheel.

324
00:11:11,864 --> 00:11:12,871
It doesn't move.

325
00:11:12,871 --> 00:11:14,295
Not even a little.

326
00:11:14,732 --> 00:11:16,881
Behind you, the plain figure has come

327
00:11:16,881 --> 00:11:20,019
down the stairs, one slow step at a time,

328
00:11:20,019 --> 00:11:22,968
with the blanket around its shoulders.

329
00:11:22,968 --> 00:11:24,141
It looks at the gate.

330
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:26,133
Then it picks up the kettle

331
00:11:26,133 --> 00:11:27,342
you set down by the wheel,

332
00:11:27,342 --> 00:11:29,031
and moves it exactly one step.

333
00:11:29,486 --> 00:11:30,599
Closer to the gate.

334
00:11:30,599 --> 00:11:32,903
You don't need it to draw anything.

335
00:11:33,422 --> 00:11:34,604
On day 172,

336
00:11:34,604 --> 00:11:37,829
the wheel moves a finger's width.

337
00:11:37,829 --> 00:11:40,659
It has taken three days to get it there.

338
00:11:40,659 --> 00:11:42,233
You build small fires

339
00:11:42,233 --> 00:11:44,137
against the iron, to warm it.

340
00:11:44,137 --> 00:11:45,647
You pour boiling water

341
00:11:45,647 --> 00:11:47,211
into the teeth of the rack.

342
00:11:47,211 --> 00:11:49,279
You chip the ice away from the gate

343
00:11:49,279 --> 00:11:49,994
with the saw,

344
00:11:49,994 --> 00:11:53,587
until your hands crack and bleed a little at the knuckles.

345
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,194
Then you light another fire.

346
00:11:55,194 --> 00:11:57,397
The striped figure stands on the ice,

347
00:11:57,397 --> 00:12:00,186
outside the gap, and watches you work.

348
00:12:00,186 --> 00:12:02,067
It doesn't stop you.

349
00:12:02,067 --> 00:12:03,076
It doesn't help.

350
00:12:03,076 --> 00:12:05,158
But it doesn't leave, either.

351
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:07,516
Once, when you look up from the gate,

352
00:12:07,516 --> 00:12:08,364
it's watching the

353
00:12:08,364 --> 00:12:10,466
plain figure through the window.

354
00:12:10,466 --> 00:12:12,865
And you understand that whatever you're doing,

355
00:12:12,865 --> 00:12:14,826
it wants the same thing you do.

356
00:12:14,826 --> 00:12:17,426
It just can't be the one to do it.

357
00:12:17,848 --> 00:12:18,916
On the third night,

358
00:12:18,916 --> 00:12:21,785
the fire steel slips out of Mara's frozen fingers.

359
00:12:21,785 --> 00:12:23,793
It drops into the fishing hole,

360
00:12:23,793 --> 00:12:26,384
and sinks, like the lantern in the lock.

361
00:12:26,384 --> 00:12:28,448
Nobody says anything for a while.

362
00:12:28,901 --> 00:12:30,600
Then you take out the box.

363
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,592
Four matches.

364
00:12:31,965 --> 00:12:32,532
On day 100,

365
00:12:32,532 --> 00:12:35,201
you kept them, because some habits are earned.

366
00:12:35,735 --> 00:12:37,047
Tonight, they earn it.

367
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:38,000
You strike one,

368
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,816
cupped in both hands, and the gate fire catches.

369
00:12:41,816 --> 00:12:42,336
Three.

370
00:12:42,857 --> 00:12:44,317
In the morning, you lean on the

371
00:12:44,317 --> 00:12:46,162
wheel with everything you have.

372
00:12:46,162 --> 00:12:46,795
It moves.

373
00:12:46,795 --> 00:12:48,250
Just a finger's width.

374
00:12:48,250 --> 00:12:50,083
It's the first thing that has

375
00:12:50,083 --> 00:12:51,714
moved on this island in weeks.

376
00:12:51,714 --> 00:12:54,135
You count the food that night.

377
00:12:54,135 --> 00:12:54,888
Two tins.

378
00:12:54,888 --> 00:12:56,393
One bag of flour.

379
00:12:56,393 --> 00:12:58,325
Two fish from the hole,

380
00:12:58,325 --> 00:12:59,667
if you're lucky tomorrow.

381
00:12:59,667 --> 00:13:01,103
You've been hungrier.

382
00:13:01,461 --> 00:13:04,089
You can't remember when.

383
00:13:04,089 --> 00:13:05,745
On day 175,

384
00:13:05,745 --> 00:13:07,650
you draw your plan for the plain figure.

385
00:13:07,650 --> 00:13:09,495
You're the worst artist on the island,

386
00:13:09,495 --> 00:13:10,754
and everybody knows it.

387
00:13:10,754 --> 00:13:12,313
But you draw it anyway.

388
00:13:12,702 --> 00:13:14,283
The sluice gate, open.

389
00:13:14,283 --> 00:13:15,827
Water rushing.

390
00:13:15,827 --> 00:13:18,071
The ring on the ice, broken.

391
00:13:18,071 --> 00:13:20,046
A boat, with two figures in it,

392
00:13:20,046 --> 00:13:22,056
going away down the river.

393
00:13:22,477 --> 00:13:24,994
And on the ice, a plain figure,

394
00:13:24,994 --> 00:13:28,822
walking out through the gap, toward a striped one.

395
00:13:28,822 --> 00:13:30,341
Two circles, joined.

396
00:13:30,341 --> 00:13:31,867
You give it the pencil.

397
00:13:31,867 --> 00:13:35,140
It looks at your drawing for a long time.

398
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:36,818
Then, under your boat,

399
00:13:36,818 --> 00:13:39,120
it draws two joined circles.

400
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:42,026
Under itself and the striped figure,

401
00:13:42,026 --> 00:13:43,372
it draws two more.

402
00:13:43,372 --> 00:13:45,113
And then it draws one

403
00:13:45,113 --> 00:13:47,390
short line beneath both pairs.

404
00:13:47,390 --> 00:13:49,200
Mara knows what that means.

405
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,546
It's the line she

406
00:13:50,546 --> 00:13:52,540
drew under two, on day 88.

407
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:55,053
It means: whatever happens.

408
00:13:55,053 --> 00:13:57,197
Nobody draws anything else.

409
00:13:57,634 --> 00:13:59,743
There's nothing else to say.

410
00:13:59,743 --> 00:14:01,949
That night, you pack the boat.

411
00:14:01,949 --> 00:14:02,808
The blankets,

412
00:14:02,808 --> 00:14:05,193
the kettle, the bottles, the tin.

413
00:14:05,502 --> 00:14:05,989
The can,

414
00:14:05,989 --> 00:14:08,564
still tied on behind, still signed twice.

415
00:14:08,938 --> 00:14:10,060
You leave the last candle

416
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:11,052
burning in the window,

417
00:14:11,052 --> 00:14:14,517
because it doesn't matter anymore who sees it.

418
00:14:14,517 --> 00:14:17,559
On day 178, the ship arrives.

419
00:14:17,559 --> 00:14:20,274
The straight edge slides over the island,

420
00:14:20,274 --> 00:14:21,349
and every shadow

421
00:14:21,349 --> 00:14:23,673
on the snow disappears at once.

422
00:14:24,128 --> 00:14:25,536
Just like the forecourt,

423
00:14:25,536 --> 00:14:28,016
on the evening you tried to pay for milk.

424
00:14:28,016 --> 00:14:30,936
The ring on the ice glows brighter,

425
00:14:30,936 --> 00:14:32,716
as if someone turned it up.

426
00:14:32,716 --> 00:14:34,789
The striped figure stands at the

427
00:14:34,789 --> 00:14:36,901
gap with the silver case at its feet.

428
00:14:36,901 --> 00:14:38,556
Its scanner is lowered.

429
00:14:38,556 --> 00:14:40,057
It looks at the sky,

430
00:14:40,057 --> 00:14:44,011
then at the mill, then at the sky again.

431
00:14:44,011 --> 00:14:45,855
All along the river,

432
00:14:45,855 --> 00:14:48,443
the last craft are coming down.

433
00:14:48,443 --> 00:14:50,771
At the bend, the big ring is

434
00:14:50,771 --> 00:14:52,521
full of pairs,

435
00:14:52,521 --> 00:14:55,704
standing very still under the edge of the ship.

436
00:14:55,704 --> 00:14:57,370
You have two days.

437
00:14:57,370 --> 00:14:58,604
You don't sleep.

438
00:14:58,604 --> 00:15:01,236
You and Mara take turns on the wheel,

439
00:15:01,236 --> 00:15:03,916
all night, by the light of the gate fire.

440
00:15:04,402 --> 00:15:05,636
Two matches.

441
00:15:05,636 --> 00:15:06,534
Then one.

442
00:15:06,534 --> 00:15:08,597
By dawn on day 179,

443
00:15:08,597 --> 00:15:11,787
the gate is open a hand's width.

444
00:15:12,241 --> 00:15:14,553
Water spits through the gap underneath it,

445
00:15:14,553 --> 00:15:15,875
white and furious.

446
00:15:16,392 --> 00:15:18,361
The ice in the channel groans.

447
00:15:18,361 --> 00:15:20,336
But it doesn't break.

448
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:21,238
Not yet.

449
00:15:21,238 --> 00:15:24,892
On day 180, you open the gate.

450
00:15:24,892 --> 00:15:27,612
All three of you, on the wheel.

451
00:15:27,612 --> 00:15:29,002
You, Mara,

452
00:15:29,002 --> 00:15:31,646
and the plain figure, gray as ash,

453
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:34,869
leaning its whole weight on the iron beside you.

454
00:15:34,869 --> 00:15:36,174
The wheel turns.

455
00:15:36,533 --> 00:15:37,034
Once.

456
00:15:37,034 --> 00:15:37,618
Twice.

457
00:15:37,618 --> 00:15:40,563
The gate lifts out of the water,

458
00:15:40,563 --> 00:15:42,301
and the river comes through.

459
00:15:42,301 --> 00:15:45,422
It hits the ice in the channel from underneath,

460
00:15:45,422 --> 00:15:46,662
and the ice breaks with a

461
00:15:46,662 --> 00:15:48,825
sound like a tree splitting in half.

462
00:15:48,825 --> 00:15:52,069
Slabs tilt and spin away downstream.

463
00:15:52,524 --> 00:15:54,261
Black water opens behind them,

464
00:15:54,261 --> 00:15:56,355
all the way down to the river.

465
00:15:56,761 --> 00:15:58,448
And where the water shows,

466
00:15:58,448 --> 00:15:59,935
the band flickers.

467
00:16:00,534 --> 00:16:01,710
And goes out.

468
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,390
The ring is broken.

469
00:16:03,390 --> 00:16:06,073
You push the boat into the channel,

470
00:16:06,073 --> 00:16:07,961
and climb in, and grab the oars.

471
00:16:08,495 --> 00:16:09,785
Mara turns around.

472
00:16:09,785 --> 00:16:11,143
The plain figure is

473
00:16:11,143 --> 00:16:13,602
standing on the bank of the island.

474
00:16:13,602 --> 00:16:15,316
The striped figure has come

475
00:16:15,316 --> 00:16:16,750
through the gap to meet it.

476
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:18,687
It holds out the silver case.

477
00:16:18,687 --> 00:16:20,411
The plain figure takes it.

478
00:16:20,411 --> 00:16:22,297
It opens it, and kneels,

479
00:16:22,297 --> 00:16:26,762
slowly, at the edge of the water, right beside your boat.

480
00:16:26,762 --> 00:16:29,453
It sets down a small marker on the ice.

481
00:16:29,453 --> 00:16:32,072
Two circles, joined by a short line.

482
00:16:32,072 --> 00:16:35,196
The striped figure looks at the marker.

483
00:16:35,196 --> 00:16:36,753
Then it turns away.

484
00:16:36,753 --> 00:16:39,578
On day one, you watched this happen from

485
00:16:39,578 --> 00:16:42,299
behind a counter, and didn't understand it.

486
00:16:42,673 --> 00:16:43,606
Now you do.

487
00:16:43,606 --> 00:16:44,927
Already counted.

488
00:16:44,927 --> 00:16:46,374
Leave these two.

489
00:16:47,073 --> 00:16:48,695
The plain figure closes

490
00:16:48,695 --> 00:16:50,318
its case and stands up.

491
00:16:50,318 --> 00:16:51,935
It looks at you.

492
00:16:51,935 --> 00:16:52,507
At Mara.

493
00:16:52,507 --> 00:16:54,351
Then the two figures walk away

494
00:16:54,351 --> 00:16:55,833
across the ice,

495
00:16:55,833 --> 00:16:58,340
side by side, toward the ring at the bend,

496
00:16:58,340 --> 00:17:01,249
where one last small craft is waiting.

497
00:17:01,249 --> 00:17:04,577
Halfway there, the plain figure stops.

498
00:17:04,577 --> 00:17:06,357
It turns around.

499
00:17:06,357 --> 00:17:08,165
And it raises one arm.

500
00:17:08,165 --> 00:17:08,951
It waves.

501
00:17:08,951 --> 00:17:11,406
Mara stands up in the boat,

502
00:17:11,406 --> 00:17:14,689
so fast it rocks, and waves back with both arms,

503
00:17:14,689 --> 00:17:17,018
long after it has turned away.

504
00:17:17,018 --> 00:17:17,845
On day 75,

505
00:17:17,845 --> 00:17:21,822
she wrote: we called out, they waved.

506
00:17:21,822 --> 00:17:24,785
This time, it was the other way around.

507
00:17:24,785 --> 00:17:26,159
The two figures walk on,

508
00:17:26,159 --> 00:17:28,615
and climb into the craft together.

509
00:17:28,615 --> 00:17:29,300
It lifts.

510
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:32,015
Above you, the ship begins to rise.

511
00:17:32,015 --> 00:17:32,875
Slowly.

512
00:17:33,185 --> 00:17:33,897
Silently.

513
00:17:33,897 --> 00:17:35,962
Its straight edge pulls back

514
00:17:35,962 --> 00:17:37,498
across the sky,

515
00:17:37,498 --> 00:17:40,427
and every shadow on the snow comes back at once.

516
00:17:40,427 --> 00:17:41,662
The trees.

517
00:17:41,662 --> 00:17:42,619
The mill.

518
00:17:42,619 --> 00:17:43,576
The boat.

519
00:17:43,576 --> 00:17:44,355
You.

520
00:17:44,954 --> 00:17:47,352
You watch until the ship is a dark line,

521
00:17:47,352 --> 00:17:49,172
then a dot, then nothing.

522
00:17:49,691 --> 00:17:51,897
For the first time in a hundred and eighty days,

523
00:17:51,897 --> 00:17:54,887
there's nothing in the sky but sky.

524
00:17:54,887 --> 00:17:58,230
Pale, wintry, ordinary blue.

525
00:17:58,230 --> 00:18:01,561
At the bend, the big ring has gone dark.

526
00:18:01,561 --> 00:18:02,770
Around the island,

527
00:18:02,770 --> 00:18:05,333
the broken band lies on the ice in pieces,

528
00:18:05,333 --> 00:18:07,475
and one by one, the pieces fade.

529
00:18:07,994 --> 00:18:09,624
You let the current take the boat

530
00:18:09,624 --> 00:18:10,487
down the channel,

531
00:18:10,487 --> 00:18:14,152
out onto the river, through floating slabs of ice.

532
00:18:14,152 --> 00:18:15,871
Neither of you rows.

533
00:18:16,198 --> 00:18:17,592
Neither of you can.

534
00:18:17,592 --> 00:18:20,177
Mara unrolls the ledger to see

535
00:18:20,177 --> 00:18:22,125
what the plain figure drew last.

536
00:18:22,125 --> 00:18:23,888
It's at the very end,

537
00:18:23,888 --> 00:18:26,217
after the line under the two pairs.

538
00:18:26,217 --> 00:18:28,065
The ship, going up.

539
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:29,791
A row of short lines.

540
00:18:29,791 --> 00:18:32,287
And an arrow, pointing down.

541
00:18:32,887 --> 00:18:36,133
Mara counts the lines out loud.

542
00:18:36,133 --> 00:18:36,539
Sixty.

543
00:18:36,539 --> 00:18:37,752
Day 240.

544
00:18:38,353 --> 00:18:39,157
It isn't over.

545
00:18:39,157 --> 00:18:40,521
It's coming back.
